From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coop-fetch <coop-fetch@localhost>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op pose play: the game's AS play request to the module

One more wrapped game function in patch 0005's table
(nx2/coop_world_wraps.py WRAPS; its id in host/hos_coop_pose_play.h), for
oot-remake-multiplayer's 0.12.1 downed-move root fix:
- 32: main+0x2022a0, play an AS command on an actor (x0 the request:
  +0 actor, +8 the command's name, +0x10 slot; returns 1 when played,
  and 1 unplayed when skip-if-same is set and the slot already plays
  it). 87 call sites, the player's state steps among them. A downed
  Link held in a lying pose was turned back to the game's Wait by its
  ground verbs' own plays every frame, so he stood and flickered.
The module answers 1 (as played) for its own downed Link held in a
lying pose, slot 0, any command but the pose (and a horse's); every
other call runs the game's play. Nothing else changes: the wrap
machinery, the checks (build id, first words) and the hello's bits are
0005's.
---
 host/hos_coop_pose_play.h | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++
 nx2/coop_world_wraps.py   |  4 ++++
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 host/hos_coop_pose_play.h

diff --git a/host/hos_coop_pose_play.h b/host/hos_coop_pose_play.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0000000
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/hos_coop_pose_play.h
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+   The game's AS play request, on Hookshot (oot-remake-multiplayer, docs/play-online.md "Down but not out", the 0.12.1
+   downed-move root fix).
+
+   One wrapped game function more in the one wrap table (patch 0005's nx2/coop_world_wraps.py WRAPS; the id is in the
+   one wrap space of hos_coop_world.h). Patch 0049 adds its row and this file (Hookshot's host/hos_coop_pose_play.h is
+   the same file). The module's hos_coop_wrap gets it; Hookshot announces it in HOS_COOP_WORLD_HELLO's bits. The row:
+     (32, 0x2022a0, (0xd503237f, 0xd10203ff, 0xa9047bfd, 0xf9002bf7, 0xa90657f6, 0xa9074ff4)),
+   Plain C. */
+#ifndef HOS_COOP_POSE_PLAY_H
+#define HOS_COOP_POSE_PLAY_H
+
+/* main+0x2022a0: play an AS command on an actor (x0 the request: +0 actor, +8 char* command, +0x10 s32 slot, +0x14
+   rate, +0x18 / +0x1c, +0x20 u8 skip-if-same, +0x28 node; docs/addresses.md kComponentsAs, the puppets' kPlayAs).
+   Returns a bool: 1 when played, and 1 without playing when skip-if-same is set and the slot already plays that
+   command (main+0x2023a0 .. +0x2023d0 compare the names, both go to main+0x2025c8 = mov w20, #1). 87 call sites in
+   the game (tools/game_scan/callers.py), the player's state steps among them. The module answers 1 (as played) for its
+   own downed Link held in a lying pose, slot 0, any command but the pose (and a horse's): the game's ground verbs
+   (Walk / Wait) keep moving him from the stick while the pose stays on screen. Every other call runs the game's
+   play. */
+#define HOS_COOP_WRAP_POSE_PLAY 32u
+
+#endif
diff --git a/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py b/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
+++ b/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
@@ -71,4 +71,8 @@ WRAPS = (
     # HOS_COOP_WRAP_CRAWL_ROOM (patch 0046): the crawl's room-to-stand-up check (x0 the player actor; returns a
     # bool). The module answers 0 (no room) for its own downed Link only, so the game's crawl lasts the down
     (31, 0x301ac50, (0xd503237f, 0xa9bd7bfd, 0xf9000bfc, 0xa9024ff4, 0x910003fd, 0xd13b03ff)),  # pacibsp; stp x29, x30, [sp, #-0x30]!; str x28; stp x20, x19; mov x29, sp; sub sp, sp, #0xec0
+    # HOS_COOP_WRAP_POSE_PLAY (patch 0049): the game's AS play request (x0 the request; returns a bool). The module
+    # answers 1 (as played, the request's own skip-if-same answer) for its own downed Link held in a lying pose, slot 0,
+    # any command but the pose, so the game's ground verbs move him without turning him back to their Wait
+    (32, 0x2022a0, (0xd503237f, 0xd10203ff, 0xa9047bfd, 0xf9002bf7, 0xa90657f6, 0xa9074ff4)),  # pacibsp; sub sp, sp, #0x80; stp x29, x30, [sp, #0x40]; str x23, [sp, #0x50]; stp x22, x21, [sp, #0x60]; stp x20, x19, [sp, #0x70]
 )


